WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:03.400
Zana · Agentforce Studio in Zana

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:07.354
Building agents used to be complicated and painful.

00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:14.612
Meet Agentforce Studio in Zana: build,
test, and fix your agents in one place.

00:00:14.801 --> 00:00:22.239
Here's Northstar Support, open in Agentforce Studio: real
Agent Script, with a compiler that checks every line.

00:00:22.420 --> 00:00:25.671
Graph view shows the whole conversation at a glance.

00:00:26.800 --> 00:00:31.263
Each action opens in its own
tab, down to the Apex behind it,

00:00:31.444 --> 00:00:34.508
and the Flow, drawn as its real canvas.

00:00:34.689 --> 00:00:40.546
The order lookup returns a Lightning Type: its
schema, and the card component that renders it.

00:00:40.727 --> 00:00:50.051
Compile, then preview. Can I return an item after twenty-one
days? The agent says fourteen days. Our policy is thirty.

00:00:50.232 --> 00:01:00.894
Now hand it to the agent. Ask for test scenarios, and they land in the shared
Scenarios tab, each with a persona, a goal and the criteria a judge will check.

00:01:01.076 --> 00:01:06.404
Ask it to run them. Three customers,
in parallel, each scored by the judge.

00:01:07.155 --> 00:01:12.049
Two pass. The judge shows exactly
why the return policy failed.

00:01:12.232 --> 00:01:19.023
Ask it to improve the failing one. It tests every attempt
against the same batch, without touching your file.

00:01:23.227 --> 00:01:26.490
Baseline two of three. Best, three of three.

00:01:26.671 --> 00:01:30.907
You review the change as a diff. Accept it, and save.

00:01:31.532 --> 00:01:36.740
Ask it to check again: thirty days. And
the batch now passes, three of three.

00:01:40.534 --> 00:01:48.008
That's Agentforce Studio. Build, see, test, and
fix your agents, with the evidence to ship them.
